<xml xmlns="https://developers.google.com/blockly/xml"><variables><variable id="v_joy_x">joy_x</variable><variable id="v_paddle_speed">paddle_speed</variable><variable id="v_paddle_x">paddle_x</variable><variable id="v_ball_x">ball_x</variable><variable id="v_ball_y">ball_y</variable><variable id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</variable><variable id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</variable><variable id="v_bricks">bricks</variable><variable id="v_score">score</variable><variable id="v_lives">lives</variable><variable id="v_row">row</variable><variable id="v_col">col</variable><variable id="v_idx">idx</variable></variables><block type="program_start" id="arkanoid_start" x="-74" y="59"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Main program start. Here the display, joystick and all game variables are prepared once. The game itself then runs in the PROGRAM LOOP block.</comment><next><block type="oled_init" id="arkanoid_oled_init"><mutation xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" display_type="AUTO"></mutation><field name="DISPLAY_TYPE">AUTO</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">OLED display initialization 128&#215;64. AUTO mode lets ESP IDE select the supported OLED driver; pins SDA=21 and SCL=22 are taken from the default project and can be changed according to the board.</comment><value name="SDA_PIN"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0001"><field name="NUM">21</field></shadow></value><value name="SCL_PIN"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0002"><field name="NUM">22</field></shadow></value><next><block type="joystick_init" id="arkanoid_joystick_init"><field name="joy_name">1</field><field name="rot">270</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Joystick 1 initialization. For Arkanoid, we only use the X-axis; the value is approximately -100 on the left, 0 in the middle and +100 on the right.</comment><value name="vrx"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0003"><field name="NUM">13</field></shadow></value><value name="vry"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0004"><field name="NUM">14</field></shadow></value><value name="sw"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0005"><field name="NUM">15</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0007"><field name="VAR" id="v_joy_x">joy_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Default joystick axis value. Zero corresponds to the center position and prevents the use of an undefined value before the first reading of the joystick.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0006"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0009"><field name="VAR" id="v_paddle_x">paddle_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The starting X coordinates of the paddle. The paddle width is 20px, so the value 54 places it approximately in the middle of the 128px display.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0008"><field name="NUM">54</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0011"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Initial X coordinates of the ball. The ball is 4 px wide and starts approximately in the middle of the display.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0010"><field name="NUM">62</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0013"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The starting Y coordinates of the ball. A value of 48 places the ball above the paddle and below the bricks field.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0012"><field name="NUM">48</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0015"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Horizontal speed of the ball. A value of +2 indicates a movement of 2 pixels to the right in each passage of the main loop.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0014"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0017"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Vertical speed of the ball. A value of -2 indicates a movement of 2 pixels up in each loop pass. The sign determines the direction.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0016"><field name="NUM">-2</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0021"><field name="VAR" id="v_bricks">bricks</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Creates a status field for all 24 bricks. Each item has a value of 1 at the beginning = the brick exists; after the hit it changes to 0.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="lists_repeat" id="b0020"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Repeats the value of 1 24 times in total, because the playing field has 3 rows &#215; 8 columns = 24 bricks.</comment><value name="ITEM"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0018"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><value name="NUM"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0019"><field name="NUM">24</field></shadow></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0023"><field name="VAR" id="v_score">score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The player&#39;s initial score. One point is added for each bricks destroyed; the maximum score for one round is 24.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0022"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0025"><field name="VAR" id="v_lives">lives</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The number of lives at the beginning of the game. When the ball falls below the bottom edge of the display, one life is deducted.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0024"><field name="NUM">3</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0027"><field name="VAR" id="v_row">row</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Auxiliary variable row. It is used to calculate the row of the affected brick and also when rendering all rows.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0026"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0029"><field name="VAR" id="v_col">col</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Auxiliary variable col. It is used to calculate the column of the affected brick and also when rendering all columns.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0028"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0031"><field name="VAR" id="v_idx">idx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Auxiliary variable idx. Converts a row/col pair to a single index in a one-dimensional bricks array.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0030"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block><block type="program_loop" id="arkanoid_loop" x="690" y="50"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Main game loop. First, it loads the joystick and calculates the relative speed of the paddle from its deflection. The paddle moves by the calculated number of pixels and its position is limited to the display. Then the ball is moved, collisions and the state of play are resolved and finally a new framebuffer is assembled. The ball is drawn in front of an opaque paddle.</comment><statement name="DO"><block type="variables_set" id="b0033"><field name="VAR" id="v_joy_x">joy_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Retrieves the current X-axis offset of the joystick into the joy_x variable. The value no longer determines the absolute position of the paddle; in subsequent blocks, we calculate the direction and speed of relative movement from it.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="get_joy_axis_ble" id="b0032"><field name="joy_name">1</field><field name="axis">X</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Reading the X-axis of joystick # 1. The ESP IDE returns an approximate range of -100 to +100. The greater the absolute deflection from zero, the faster the paddle will move.</comment></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b_rel_speed_set"><field name="VAR" id="v_paddle_speed">paddle_speed</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Converts joystick deflection to paddle speed. When dividing by 20, approximately -5 to +5 px is obtained for the passage through the loop. A smaller divisor means a faster/more sensitive paddle, a larger divisor means a slower movement.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_round" id="b_rel_speed_round"><field name="OP">ROUND</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Rounds the calculated speed to whole pixels. The normal rounding makes the steering symmetrical for both left and right movement.</comment><value name="NUM"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b_rel_speed_div"><field name="OP">DIVIDE</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Divides the deflection of the joystick by 20. For example, +100 → +5 px, +40 → +2 px, -60 → -3 px for one pass through the loop.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b_rel_joy_speed"><field name="VAR" id="v_joy_x">joy_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n_rel_speed_divisor"><field name="NUM">25</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b_rel_paddle_set"><field name="VAR" id="v_paddle_x">paddle_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Relatively shifts the paddle: adds paddle_speed to its current paddle_x position. Thus, the joystick does not determine the place on the display, but the speed and direction of movement.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_constrain" id="b_rel_paddle_constrain"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Limits the new paddle position to 0…108. The paddle is 20px wide, so at X=108 it ends exactly at the right edge of the 128px display.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b_rel_paddle_add"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Read the current position of the paddle and the speed calculated from the joystick. Positive speed shifts to the right, negative to the left.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b_rel_paddle_old"><field name="VAR" id="v_paddle_x">paddle_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="variables_get" id="b_rel_speed_get"><field name="VAR" id="v_paddle_speed">paddle_speed</field></block></value></block></value><value name="LOW"><shadow type="math_number" id="n_rel_paddle_low"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><value name="HIGH"><shadow type="math_number" id="n_rel_paddle_high"><field name="NUM">108</field></shadow></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0049"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Updates the horizontal position of the ball: ball_x = ball_x + ball_dx. At a speed of &#177;2, the ball moves two pixels per frame.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0048"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The sum of the current X coordinate of the ball and the horizontal velocity of ball_dx.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0046"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="variables_get" id="b0047"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field></block></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0053"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Updates the vertical position of the ball: ball_y = ball_y + ball_dy.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0052"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The sum of the current Y-coordinate of the ball and the vertical velocity of ball_dy.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0050"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="variables_get" id="b0051"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field></block></value></block></value><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0061"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Collision with the left wall. When the left edge of the ball reaches X=0, return it to X=0 and change the direction of movement to the right.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0060"><field name="OP">LT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0058"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0059"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0055"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting the left wall, it aligns the ball exactly to X=0 so that it does not stay outside the framebuffer.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0054"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0057"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting the left wall, it sets the horizontal speed to +2, i.e. moving to the right.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0056"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0069"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Collision with the right wall. The value 123 corresponds to the last safe X position of the four-pixel ball on the 128px display.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0068"><field name="OP">GT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0066"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0067"><field name="NUM">123</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0063"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting the right wall, aligns the left edge of the ball to X=123.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0062"><field name="NUM">123</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0065"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting the right wall, it sets the horizontal speed to -2, i.e. movement to the left.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0064"><field name="NUM">-2</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0077"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Collision with the top edge of the display. When reaching the upper wall, the vertical direction changes downwards.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0076"><field name="OP">LT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0074"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0075"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0071"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Aligns the ball to the top edge of Y=0 so that it does not remain partially outside the framebuffer.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0070"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0073"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting the upper wall, it sets the vertical speed to +2, i.e. downward movement.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0072"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0105"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">First part of the paddle collision test: the ball must already be low enough, i.e. ball_y &gt; 54.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0104"><field name="OP">GT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0102"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0103"><field name="NUM">54</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0101"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Second part of the test: the ball must not yet be under the paddle. The range Y 55…59 creates a sufficiently wide collision area even at a speed of 2 px/frame.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0100"><field name="OP">LT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0098"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0099"><field name="NUM">60</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0097"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Test the left edge of the paddle. Ball_x must be more than paddle_x - 4 because the ball is 4px wide and can touch the paddle with its right edge.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0096"><field name="OP">GT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0092"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0095"><field name="OP">MINUS</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0093"><field name="VAR" id="v_paddle_x">paddle_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0094"><field name="NUM">4</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0091"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Right edge test of the paddle. Ball_x must be smaller than paddle_x + 20, i.e. the right edge of the paddle.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0090"><field name="OP">LT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0086"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0089"><field name="OP">ADD</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0087"><field name="VAR" id="v_paddle_x">paddle_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0088"><field name="NUM">20</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0085"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">We solve the collision with the paddle only when the ball actually flies down (ball_dy &gt; 0). This will prevent the ball from bouncing repeatedly inside the paddle.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0084"><field name="OP">GT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0082"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0083"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0079"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After hitting the paddle, it moves the ball to Y=55, i.e. above its drawn area. This helps prevent the ball from getting caught in the paddle.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0078"><field name="NUM">55</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0081"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Bounce off the paddle: the vertical speed is set to -2, so the ball starts to fly upwards.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0080"><field name="NUM">-2</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></statement></block></statement></block></statement></block></statement></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0153"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">We check the collision with the bricks only from Y&gt;5. Thus, the top empty edge of the display is not mistakenly considered the first row of bricks.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0152"><field name="OP">GT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0150"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0151"><field name="NUM">5</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="controls_if" id="b0149"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">The top bricks box ends before Y=24. Only in this band do we convert the coordinates of the ball to row/col and look for the affected brick.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0148"><field name="OP">LT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0146"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0147"><field name="NUM">24</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0110"><field name="VAR" id="v_col">col</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Calculates the brick column: floor(ball_x / 16). Each of the 8 columns occupies 16 px horizontally.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_round" id="b0109"><field name="OP">ROUNDDOWN</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Rounding down gives the whole number of column 0…7.</comment><value name="NUM"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0108"><field name="OP">DIVIDE</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Divides the X coordinate of the ball by a width of one column of 16 pixels.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0106"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0107"><field name="NUM">16</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0117"><field name="VAR" id="v_row">row</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Calculates the row of the brick: floor((ball_y - 6) / 6). The first row starts with Y=6 and the individual rows have a step of 6 px.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_round" id="b0116"><field name="OP">ROUNDDOWN</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Rounding down gives a row number of 0…2.</comment><value name="NUM"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0115"><field name="OP">DIVIDE</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Divide the relative Y coordinate by the height/step of the 6 px line.</comment><value name="A"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0113"><field name="OP">MINUS</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Subtract the top indent of 6 px, so that the beginning of the first row of bricks corresponds to zero.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0111"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0112"><field name="NUM">6</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0114"><field name="NUM">6</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0123"><field name="VAR" id="v_idx">idx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Converts row/col to a linear index: idx = row &#215; 8 + col. This allows one brick to be found in a one-dimensional bricks array.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0122"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Adding col results in an index of a specific brick in the range of 0...23.</comment><value name="A"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0120"><field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Each completed row contains 8 bricks, so we multiply the row by eight.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0118"><field name="VAR" id="v_row">row</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0119"><field name="NUM">8</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="B"><block type="variables_get" id="b0121"><field name="VAR" id="v_col">col</field></block></value></block></value><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0145"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Verifies that there is still a brick on the calculated position. Value 1 means active brick; value 0 already destroyed.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0130"><field name="OP">EQ</field><value name="A"><block type="lists_getIndex" id="b0127"><mutation statement="false" at="true"></mutation><field name="MODE">GET</field><field name="WHERE">FROM_START</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">It reads the state of the bricks from the bricks field. Blockly here uses the position from the beginning of the field; therefore, 1 is added to the internal idx 0…23.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="variables_get" id="b0128"><field name="VAR" id="v_bricks">bricks</field></block></value><value name="AT"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0126"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Converting Internal Index 0…23 to 1 position 1…24 used by this Blockly Block List.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0124"><field name="VAR" id="v_idx">idx</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0125"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0129"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="lists_setIndex" id="b0135"><mutation at="true"></mutation><field name="MODE">SET</field><field name="WHERE">FROM_START</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After the hit, it sets the state of a specific bricks in the bricks field to 0. On subsequent slides, this brick no longer draws or collides.</comment><value name="LIST"><block type="variables_get" id="b0136"><field name="VAR" id="v_bricks">bricks</field></block></value><value name="AT"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0133"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Just like when reading, idx converts 0…23 to a one position in the Blockly list.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0131"><field name="VAR" id="v_idx">idx</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0132"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="TO"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0134"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0140"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Reverses the vertical speed of the ball using 0 - ball_dy. Thanks to this, the speed size of 2 px is maintained and only the direction is changed.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0139"><field name="OP">MINUS</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Mathematical notation of sign change: 0 - ball_dy. For +2 there will be -2 and for -2 there will be +2.</comment><value name="A"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0137"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><value name="B"><block type="variables_get" id="b0138"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field></block></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0144"><field name="VAR" id="v_score">score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Raises the score by 1 for the destroyed bricks.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0143"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Calculation of the new score: score + 1.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0141"><field name="VAR" id="v_score">score</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0142"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0173"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Victory check. Once score &gt; 23, all 24 bricks have been destroyed and a new round is prepared.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0172"><field name="OP">GT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0170"><field name="VAR" id="v_score">score</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0171"><field name="NUM">23</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0157"><field name="VAR" id="v_bricks">bricks</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">On winning, it creates a new array of 24 active bricks, so the next complete playing area begins.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="lists_repeat" id="b0156"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Creates 24 ones to reset all bricks after a win.</comment><value name="ITEM"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0154"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><value name="NUM"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0155"><field name="NUM">24</field></shadow></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0159"><field name="VAR" id="v_score">score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After winning, he resets the score for the new round.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0158"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0161"><field name="VAR" id="v_lives">lives</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After winning, the player restores three lives.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0160"><field name="NUM">3</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0163"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After winning, he returns the ball to the center on the starting X coordinate.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0162"><field name="NUM">62</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0165"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After winning, he returns the ball to the starting Y coordinate above the paddle.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0164"><field name="NUM">48</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0167"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After winning, he sets the horizontal speed to +2.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0166"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0169"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After winning, he sets the vertical speed to -2, so the new round starts with an upward movement.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0168"><field name="NUM">-2</field></shadow></value></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0201"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Missed ball detection. If ball_y &gt; 63, the ball has already left the bottom edge of the 64px display and the player loses his life.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0200"><field name="OP">GT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0198"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0199"><field name="NUM">63</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0177"><field name="VAR" id="v_lives">lives</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Subtract one life: lives = lives - 1.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0176"><field name="OP">MINUS</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Calculation of the new number of lives after the lost ball.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0174"><field name="VAR" id="v_lives">lives</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0175"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0179"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After losing his life, he returns the ball to the starting X position.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0178"><field name="NUM">62</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0181"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After losing his life, he returns the ball to the starting Y position.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0180"><field name="NUM">48</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0183"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dx">ball_dx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After the loss of life, it sets the horizontal speed again to +2.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0182"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0185"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_dy">ball_dy</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">After the loss of life, he sets the vertical speed to -2, so the new ball goes up.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0184"><field name="NUM">-2</field></shadow></value><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0197"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">GAME OVER check. When lives fall below 1 after deduction, the game will be completely restarted.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0196"><field name="OP">LT</field><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0194"><field name="VAR" id="v_lives">lives</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0195"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="variables_set" id="b0187"><field name="VAR" id="v_lives">lives</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Restores the number of lives to 3 during GAME OVER.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0186"><field name="NUM">3</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0189"><field name="VAR" id="v_score">score</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Resets the score when GAME OVER is played.</comment><value name="VALUE"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0188"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><next><block type="variables_set" id="b0193"><field name="VAR" id="v_bricks">bricks</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Restores all 24 bricks during GAME OVER.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="lists_repeat" id="b0192"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Creates a new array of 24 ones for all active bricks after GAME OVER.</comment><value name="ITEM"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0190"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><value name="NUM"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0191"><field name="NUM">24</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement><next><block type="fb_fill" id="b0202"><field name="barva">0</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Clears the entire framebuffer with color 0 before rendering a new frame. Without this step, old pixels would remain behind moving objects.</comment><next><block type="fb_draw_pic" id="}L?A[iTOi-iO}t|/XgM3"><field name="name">Ball_4x4</field><field name="alpha">-1</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Draws a 4&#215;4px ball into the framebuffer. IMPORTANT: the ball is drawn in front of the paddle, because the image used does not have transparency and the paddle should be on top when overlapped.</comment><value name="px"><block type="variables_get" id="#)_~VL/HZm@xp:m4]mX8"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_x">ball_x</field></block></value><value name="py"><block type="variables_get" id="T|YzX7T?xd;7FVpj^}Wn"><field name="VAR" id="v_ball_y">ball_y</field></block></value><value name="data"><shadow type="text" id=")!*{sp[QUL!mLP=p_X6r"><field name="TEXT">bytearray(b'\x06\x0f\x0f\x06'), 4, 8</field></shadow></value><next><block type="controls_for" id="b0236"><field name="VAR" id="v_row">row</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Outer render loop for 3 rows of bricks: row = 0…2.</comment><value name="FROM"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0233"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><value name="TO"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0234"><field name="NUM">2</field></shadow></value><value name="BY"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0235"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><statement name="DO"><block type="controls_for" id="b0232"><field name="VAR" id="v_col">col</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Internal render loop for 8 columns in each row: col = 0…7.</comment><value name="FROM"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0229"><field name="NUM">0</field></shadow></value><value name="TO"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0230"><field name="NUM">7</field></shadow></value><value name="BY"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0231"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><statement name="DO"><block type="variables_set" id="b0208"><field name="VAR" id="v_idx">idx</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">For the current row/col, the linear index idx = row &#215; 8 + col is calculated to read the state of the brick from the array.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0207"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Combines the row offset (row &#215; 8) and the Col column number into a single index.</comment><value name="A"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0205"><field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Calculates the start of the current row in the bricks: row &#215; 8 field.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0203"><field name="VAR" id="v_row">row</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0204"><field name="NUM">8</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="B"><block type="variables_get" id="b0206"><field name="VAR" id="v_col">col</field></block></value></block></value><next><block type="controls_if" id="b0228"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">It draws a brick only if its state in the bricks field still contains 1. Destroyed bricks have 0 and are skipped.</comment><value name="IF0"><block type="logic_compare" id="b0227"><field name="OP">EQ</field><value name="A"><block type="lists_getIndex" id="b0224"><mutation statement="false" at="true"></mutation><field name="MODE">GET</field><field name="WHERE">FROM_START</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">It reads the status of the current brick when rendering. 1 is added to idx due to 1 indexing of this Blockly block.</comment><value name="VALUE"><block type="variables_get" id="b0225"><field name="VAR" id="v_bricks">bricks</field></block></value><value name="AT"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0223"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Converts internal idx 0…23 to position 1…24 for reading the list.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0221"><field name="VAR" id="v_idx">idx</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0222"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0226"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></value><statement name="DO0"><block type="fb_rect_fill" id="b0220"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Draws one active brick as a filled 15&#215;5 px rectangle. The 16&#215;6 px pitch leaves a one-point gap between the bricks.</comment><value name="px"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0211"><field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">X coordinates of the brick = col &#215; 16.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0209"><field name="VAR" id="v_col">col</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0210"><field name="NUM">16</field></shadow></value></block></value><value name="py"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0216"><field name="OP">ADD</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Y coordinates of the brick = 6 + row &#215; 6. The upper 6 pixels remain as the edge of the playing area.</comment><value name="A"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0212"><field name="NUM">6</field></shadow></value><value name="B"><block type="math_arithmetic" id="b0215"><field name="OP">MULTIPLY</field><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Vertical offset of the current row of bricks: row &#215; 6.</comment><value name="A"><block type="variables_get" id="b0213"><field name="VAR" id="v_row">row</field></block></value><value name="B"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0214"><field name="NUM">6</field></shadow></value></block></value></block></value><value name="sirka"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0217"><field name="NUM">15</field></shadow></value><value name="vyska"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0218"><field name="NUM">5</field></shadow></value><value name="col"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0219"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value></block></statement></block></next></block></statement></block></statement><next><block type="fb_rect_fill" id="b0242"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Draws the bottom paddle as a full 20&#215;3 px rectangle to Y=59. It is intentionally drawn after the ball, so its opaque filling will properly cover the ball on contact.</comment><value name="px"><block type="variables_get" id="b0237"><field name="VAR" id="v_paddle_x">paddle_x</field></block></value><value name="py"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0238"><field name="NUM">59</field></shadow></value><value name="sirka"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0239"><field name="NUM">20</field></shadow></value><value name="vyska"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0240"><field name="NUM">3</field></shadow></value><value name="col"><shadow type="math_number" id="n0241"><field name="NUM">1</field></shadow></value><next><block type="oded_refresh" id="b0247"><comment pinned="false" h="110" w="520">Transfer the finished framebuffer to the OLED/simulated display. Only then will the entire currently assembled image be displayed to the user.</comment></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></next></block></statement></block>
  <!--ESPIDE_EXTENSIONS_BEGIN-->
eyJ2ZXJzaW9uIjoxLCJwcm9jZXNzb3IiOiJTaW11bGF0b3IiLCJleHRlbnNpb25zIjpbXX0=
<!--ESPIDE_EXTENSIONS_END-->
</xml>
